    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #344\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-84-implementation-audit-fixes-06-23-reacti-thr_3qr274wi23` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements #84: reactivating heartbeat occurrences under a generation protocol, closing the race where a rule edit/re-enable that recomputes an occurrence back onto an existing `cancelled` or stale-`queued` row would leave it stuck instead of firing.\n\n- Added an additive `generation integer not null default 1` column on `heartbeat_occurrences` (migration `0024_heartbeat_occurrence_generation.sql`).\n- `insertHeartbeatOccurrence` in `schedulerStore.ts` now reactivates a `cancelled` occurrence (fresh snapshot, `status='queued'`, cleared `first_started_at`/`last_error`, generation bumped, enqueued with `jobKeyMode: 'replace'`) or replaces a `queued` occurrence whose `rule_snapshot` no longer matches (in place, same id/status, generation bumped, enqueued with `jobKeyMode: 'preserve_run_at'`), while `queued`(matching)/`running`/`succeeded`/`failed` stay untouched no-ops.\n- Job payload/key now carry `generation` (`{heartbeatId, occurrenceId, generation}`, `heartbeat-fire:${heartbeatId}:${occurrenceId}:${generation}`), superseding #213's plain shape.\n- `prepareHeartbeatOccurrenceFire` checks the caller's `generation` against the row's current generation before touching any state, so a handler running against a superseded generation becomes a safe no-op rather than racing the reactivated occurrence.\n- Added integration tests covering both reactivation paths end-to-end (cancelled→reactivated, queued-stale→replaced), including an explicit assertion that a stale-generation call is a no-op while the new generation still fires exactly once. Updated existing tests for the new signature/job-key format.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm run lint` — clean\n- `pnpm run format:check` — clean\n- `pnpm run build` (full workspace typecheck) — clean\n- `pnpm run test` (unit + integration + e2e) — 679/680 passed; the one failure (`mailLiveSyncRoot.test.ts`, a `deadlock detected` in `resetDatabase`'s TRUNCATE) is confirmed pre-existing and unrelated — it reproduces identically against the pre-#84 base commit (before any of my changes existed) in an isolated worktree, and passed cleanly on a re-run against my branch.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
